<https://starwars.com#planet_DenariiStation>
        rdf:type              ies:Planet ;
        rdfs:comment          "Denarii Station was a base of laboratories and habitation modules in the Denarii Nebula—the gaseous, highly ionized remnant of a double-star system that was destroyed by the Sith Lord Naga Sadow during the Great Hyperspace War of 5000 BBY—in the Gordian Reach sector of the Trans-Hydian part of the Outer Rim Territories. It was originally used by astrophysicists for studying the nebula, but it fell into disuse centuries before 43 ABY. Nevertheless, the station was still used as a hideout by the desperate. " ;
        ies:hasName           <https://starwars.com#a4db0024-3b27-493e-a9fd-6d3e5c56bcc6> ;
        ies:inLocation        <https://starwars.com#sector_GordianReach> , <https://starwars.com#grid_P6> ;
        graphql:primaryName  "Denarii Station" .
@prefix ies:      <http://ies.data.gov.uk/ontology/ies4#> .
@prefix rdf:      <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix graphql: <http://ndtp.co.uk/ontology/> .

<https://starwars.com#planet_Deneba>
        rdf:type              ies:Planet ;
        rdfs:comment          "Deneba was a location in the galaxy. When Commerce Guild scout Tibbs Ospe discovered the planet Vandor, he figured the planet could be a stopping place for traders heading towards Deneba and Manda. By 10 BBY, Ospe fixed the ruins of Ypsobay Trading Company's headquarters and started advertising that traders could find fuel and food at Fort Ypso for their travels. At some point bartender Tivoche Bilure learned Ospe's story about Vandor and wrote it in his journal. " ;
        ies:hasName           <https://starwars.com#e70c5a6e-2d40-46d4-a084-7b4261190d15> ;
        ies:inLocation        <https://starwars.com#grid_Q13> , <https://starwars.com#sector_Maerdocia> ;
        graphql:primaryName  "Deneba" .

